;; stdlib/brawlpit/commander_mod.prn — real PARENA decision logic for BRAWLPIT's "fractal
;; commander" layer (EMILY/BACKLOG.md SECTION 419, REDGARDEN/NORTHSTAR.md §26.3's own real,
;; rule-based-first precedent: "Built instead: a real, rule-based (not learned) team-wide
;; 'Commander' signal that genuinely changes individual squad decisions, not just a spec.").
;;
;; Founder real-time: build a packet-level RL training pipeline for BRAWLPIT, applying
;; autocurriculum/league doctrine (REDGARDEN NORTHSTAR §25.4/§25.4.1) and the "fractal commander"
;; hierarchy (§26.3) but explicitly WITHOUT the squad-coordination layer (§26.3's own
;; "commander-soldier"/multi-agent nesting) -- BRAWLPIT has no teams to coordinate. This module is
;; the single-agent commander half of that hierarchy: a real, honest, rule-based posture signal
;; computed from real wire-level state (the exact fields BRAWLPIT/packages/common/protocol.h's
;; own NetPlayer struct carries), same scope discipline §26.3's own first real step used --
;; nothing here is a learned policy, it's the deterministic strategic-directive layer a low-level
;; PPO "soldier" policy conditions on, matching the doc's own "smaller in scope than the full
;; commander/soldier hierarchy... a genuine structural step in the same direction" framing.
;;
;; I32-only the whole way (no F32/struct/Vec crossing the #target boundary VS0 still can't do --
;; same real constraint stdlib/ecowar/frontier_village_mod.prn's own header names) -- damage/
;; stocks are already integer-shaped on the wire (NetPlayer.damage is a real unsigned short
;; percent, stocks a real unsigned char), and edge distance is passed pre-rounded to the nearest
;; world-unit integer by the caller (a coarse platform-fighter strategic decision doesn't need
;; sub-unit precision).
;;
;; ABI: called directly by name (commander_posture -> commander_posture) from both
;; scripts/rl_env_packet.py (via ctypes on the compiled libbrawlpit_commander.so, appending the
;; returned posture as an extra observation feature for the low-level RL policy) and, later, any
;; hand-authored/hybrid in-game bot that wants the same real strategic signal a training run saw
;; -- one real decision function, two real consumers, matching this monorepo's own standing "same
;; shape trains as ships" discipline.

(module brawlpit/commander-mod)
(export commander-posture)

;; Posture enum -- kept here as plain documented I32 constants (VS0 has no enum-to-FFI-boundary
;; story beyond int yet) rather than invented ad hoc at each call site:
;;   0 NEUTRAL   -- no strong signal either way, play it straight
;;   1 AGGRESSIVE -- meaningfully behind on stocks/damage, can't afford to sit back
;;   2 PATIENT   -- meaningfully ahead, protect the lead rather than take a risky trade
;;   3 EDGEGUARD -- opponent is off-stage/near the ledge and vulnerable, and we are safe to press
;;   4 RECOVER   -- we are ourselves off-stage/near the ledge -- survival overrides everything else

;; edge-safety checks take priority over the stock/damage read (a stock lead means nothing if
;; you're about to die off-stage, and a stock deficit means nothing if the OPPONENT is the one
;; about to die) -- this ordering is the real, deliberate strategic hierarchy a platform-fighter
;; "commander" needs that a MOBA's own lane-based posture signal never had to consider.
(defn commander-posture
    [(own-stocks : I32) (opp-stocks : I32)
     (own-damage-pct : I32) (opp-damage-pct : I32)
     (own-edge-dist : I32) (opp-edge-dist : I32)
     (edge-danger-threshold : I32)] : I32
  (if (< own-edge-dist edge-danger-threshold)
    4
    (if (< opp-edge-dist edge-danger-threshold)
      3
      (if (> own-stocks opp-stocks)
        2
        (if (< own-stocks opp-stocks)
          1
          (if (< own-damage-pct opp-damage-pct)
            2
            (if (> own-damage-pct opp-damage-pct)
              1
              0)))))))
